The legal texts come from official publications of the Republic of Angola:

  Diário da República de Angola (Imprensa Nacional), I Série, n.º 154, 16 August 2021: Lei n.º 18/21 (Lei de
  Revisão Constitucional) and the republication of the Constitution of the Republic of Angola it orders,
  https://plataformacipra.gov.ao/public/ficheiros/arquivos/Gov_AngolaConstituição190102230948141675284494.pdf
  (linked from https://governo.gov.ao/documentos/constituição), retrieved 28 October 2026;
  Diário da República de Angola, I Série, n.º 179, 11 November 2020: Lei n.º 38/20 (Código Penal Angolano) and
  Lei n.º 39/20 (Código do Processo Penal Angolano),
  https://plataformacipra.gov.ao/public/ficheiros/arquivos/Gov_AngolaLegislação982801221101131643367673.pdf,
  retrieved 28 October 2026.

The Government's portal publishes no licence for these files. They are official legal texts; their copyright
status is not confirmed here, and they are reproduced with the attribution above.

Changes made by Lexifina: the text was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line;
spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; page numbers, running heads, footnotes and their markers were removed;
headings were gathered in one structure file; and the text was arranged as git commits. The wording of the law was
not changed. None of the publishers endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
